1
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:35,000
(Blossom Through the Cloud)

2
00:01:35,001 --> 00:01:37,960
(Adapted from the novel on JJWXC,
"Landing on My Heart", by Qiao Yao)

3
00:01:38,040 --> 00:01:39,120
Thanks for your hard work, boys.

4
00:01:39,720 --> 00:01:41,960
Put it right
in the middle of the sofa.

5
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:43,240
Let me see.

6
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:44,520
A bit higher.
Further this way.

7
00:01:46,960 --> 00:01:48,239
What are you doing?

8
00:01:48,240 --> 00:01:49,319
I'm just hanging a painting.

9
00:01:49,320 --> 00:01:51,760
Look at you,
frowning and sighing like that.

10
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:55,280
You're in the way. Sit over here.

11
00:01:55,960 --> 00:01:56,999
I can't see it clearly.

12
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:58,120
Just sit over here.

13
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:00,760
I really can't stand you.

14
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:03,799
It's just a painting.

15
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:06,240
You've been fussing
over it all afternoon.

16
00:02:06,440 --> 00:02:07,440
You've made me feel like...

17
00:02:07,880 --> 00:02:08,880
- Wait, what is it?
- Hold on.

18
00:02:08,881 --> 00:02:10,000
Just like this painting.

19
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:11,560
Everything looks abstract to me now.

20
00:02:12,440 --> 00:02:14,800
Just admit you have presbyopia.

21
00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:16,720
Why blame my painting?

22
00:02:17,360 --> 00:02:19,479
The painting really reflects
the person who bought it.

23
00:02:19,480 --> 00:02:20,480
Don't move.

24
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:24,000
What are you sighing for?

25
00:02:24,001 --> 00:02:25,759
Didn't I make way for you?

26
00:02:25,760 --> 00:02:26,960
You're just in the way here!

27
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:28,839
Come on, you two.

28
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:29,920
Make him disappear. Hurry.

29
00:02:33,080 --> 00:02:34,080
I...

30
00:02:34,081 --> 00:02:35,600
What... What is going on?

31
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:38,959
Young men, come here.
Thanks for your hard work.

32
00:02:38,960 --> 00:02:39,960
Let's not hang it there anymore.

33
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:41,560
On this wall instead.

34
00:02:42,320 --> 00:02:43,320
Good.

35
00:02:43,960 --> 00:02:45,160
In the middle.
Don't move it anymore.

36
00:02:46,520 --> 00:02:47,520
Right here.

37
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:50,640
(Episode 18: Always on Your Side)

38
00:02:55,720 --> 00:02:58,240
Xiao Ruan, thank you for tonight.

39
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:01,080
What are you thanking me for?

40
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:04,280
I haven't unwound like this
in a very long time.

41
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:07,359
Thank you to both of you.

42
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:09,000
Tonight, I finally realized...

43
00:03:09,360 --> 00:03:10,640
what it's like to live for myself.

44
00:03:13,520 --> 00:03:14,520
Tonight,

45
00:03:15,280 --> 00:03:16,360
weren't you the one
who asked me out?

46
00:03:17,200 --> 00:03:18,520
If you want to thank someone,
thank yourself.

47
00:03:19,920 --> 00:03:20,920
As for the road ahead,

48
00:03:21,480 --> 00:03:23,000
I think I know which way to go now.

49
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:25,680
I'm so happy tonight.

50
00:03:26,240 --> 00:03:27,240
I want to take a stroll.

51
00:03:28,360 --> 00:03:29,360
Okay.

52
00:03:29,440 --> 00:03:30,440
Do you need me
to keep you company?

53
00:03:32,360 --> 00:03:33,360
I want...

54
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:35,120
to walk this path alone.

55
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:38,680
I'll be going then.

56
00:04:00,680 --> 00:04:01,680
(Contacts, Yue Yang)

57
00:04:01,681 --> 00:04:03,159
(Yue Yang)

58
00:04:03,160 --> 00:04:04,160
(Settings, Delete)
(Deleting the contact "Yue Yang"
will also delete your chat history.)

59
00:04:08,920 --> 00:04:10,519
(Delete Contact, Delete)

60
00:04:10,520 --> 00:04:12,000
(Processing)

61
00:04:47,880 --> 00:04:48,880
Mr. Fu.

62
00:04:49,440 --> 00:04:51,480
Stealing things? And you even
have the dog on the lookout?

63
00:04:52,320 --> 00:04:53,480
Aren't you being
a bit of a dog yourself?

64
00:04:53,920 --> 00:04:56,520
I say, Ms. He, where is
that necklace I gave you last time?

65
00:04:56,720 --> 00:04:58,000
Didn't I give it to Dong Xian?

66
00:04:58,560 --> 00:05:00,320
How many times are you going
to extort me over a necklace?

67
00:05:01,440 --> 00:05:02,680
I just forgot about that.

68
00:05:03,680 --> 00:05:05,040
There's a family gathering
the day after tomorrow.

69
00:05:06,680 --> 00:05:08,600
I'm thinking of
bringing Xiao Ruan over...

70
00:05:09,080 --> 00:05:10,080
to meet you.

71
00:05:10,920 --> 00:05:12,840
That Xiao Ruan?

72
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:18,120
Well, in what capacity?

73
00:05:18,360 --> 00:05:19,360
Take a guess.

74
00:05:20,080 --> 00:05:21,160
Quit it and just tell me.

75
00:05:21,880 --> 00:05:22,880
As my girlfriend.

76
00:05:23,280 --> 00:05:24,280
Really?

77
00:05:27,640 --> 00:05:28,640
Move aside.

78
00:05:35,040 --> 00:05:36,560
It... It doesn't have
to be too valuable.

79
00:05:41,160 --> 00:05:42,160
Here.

80
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:44,720
- Take this set.
- This one?

81
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:47,120
Isn't this the one Lester gave you?

82
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:48,400
It's too valuable.

83
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:50,720
I've been saving it
for my daughter-in-law.

84
00:05:50,880 --> 00:05:51,880
Take it.

85
00:05:52,280 --> 00:05:53,280
I'm really taking it then.

86
00:05:53,400 --> 00:05:54,480
Take it. Go on.

87
00:05:56,320 --> 00:05:57,320
The pressure is too much.

88
00:05:57,560 --> 00:05:59,319
What if I fail to marry her
and bring her home?

89
00:05:59,320 --> 00:06:00,880
You'll definitely blame me.
Won't you be heartbroken?

90
00:06:01,840 --> 00:06:02,840
Fu Ming Yu,

91
00:06:03,360 --> 00:06:05,080
if you're really that useless,

92
00:06:05,360 --> 00:06:06,399
then I'll just have to start over...

93
00:06:06,400 --> 00:06:07,400
and have another child
with your dad.

94
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:09,360
Not this again.

95
00:06:09,760 --> 00:06:10,960
It's late. Go to bed.

96
00:06:13,400 --> 00:06:14,400
Honestly.

97
00:06:15,040 --> 00:06:16,920
Then I won't disturb
you two old folks anymore.

98
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:18,480
I'm leaving.

99
00:06:21,560 --> 00:06:23,999
Wait, my goodness!
Don't climb the tree! Let's go home!

100
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:25,439
- Don't touch me.
- Do you know what time it is?

101
00:06:25,440 --> 00:06:26,760
Don't touch me!

102
00:06:29,760 --> 00:06:30,760
Didn't you say...

103
00:06:32,160 --> 00:06:33,160
that if I followed you,

104
00:06:33,840 --> 00:06:35,040
I would have enough to drink?

105
00:06:35,840 --> 00:06:36,840
Where's your integrity?

106
00:06:37,080 --> 00:06:38,239
If you're like this,

107
00:06:38,240 --> 00:06:40,320
who are you to covet
the Zheng family business?

108
00:06:40,920 --> 00:06:42,559
Why would I want
your family business?

109
00:06:42,560 --> 00:06:43,880
I just want to go home now.

110
00:06:44,240 --> 00:06:45,240
Go.

111
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:47,000
Who's stopping you?

112
00:06:47,960 --> 00:06:48,960
Who's stopping you?

113
00:06:52,320 --> 00:06:53,320
Fine.

114
00:06:54,200 --> 00:06:55,200
Tell me, my lady,

115
00:06:55,600 --> 00:06:56,600
what exactly will it take...

116
00:06:57,560 --> 00:06:58,560
to get you to go home?

117
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:01,000
You know.

118
00:07:01,160 --> 00:07:02,720
How would I know?

119
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:09,800
You...

120
00:07:10,040 --> 00:07:12,120
You can go after those influencers,

121
00:07:12,960 --> 00:07:14,960
and you can go after Ms. Ruan.

122
00:07:15,360 --> 00:07:17,360
Why is it different with me?

123
00:07:18,240 --> 00:07:20,600
Why do you hesitate with me?

124
00:07:21,800 --> 00:07:22,800
Is it because of my legs?

125
00:07:23,520 --> 00:07:24,680
You like those girls with long legs.

126
00:07:25,160 --> 00:07:26,160
My legs...

127
00:07:26,161 --> 00:07:27,920
- Careful.
- My legs are perfectly fine too!

128
00:07:28,120 --> 00:07:29,640
- Yes, they're great legs.
- I walk with such grace.

129
00:07:29,720 --> 00:07:31,560
- It's not because of your legs!
- I don't even get winded walking.

130
00:07:34,320 --> 00:07:35,400
Then why?

131
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:41,160
Say something.

132
00:07:41,760 --> 00:07:43,039
Yan An, speak up!

133
00:07:43,040 --> 00:07:44,159
You're always like this.

134
00:07:44,160 --> 00:07:45,760
- I can't stand it!
- It's because I lack confidence!

135
00:07:49,680 --> 00:07:50,880
Zheng You An, I like you.

136
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:56,080
But I know better than anyone
what kind of person I am.

137
00:07:58,720 --> 00:08:00,600
Every time I liked someone before,
I was very serious about it.

138
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:03,000
But tell me,

139
00:08:04,480 --> 00:08:05,800
how long can a relationship last?

140
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:09,800
Those other people didn't matter.
I didn't care if they left me.

141
00:08:12,040 --> 00:08:13,040
But if you were to leave,

142
00:08:16,640 --> 00:08:17,640
I really wouldn't
be able to take it.

143
00:08:21,240 --> 00:08:24,159
Besides, Mr. Zheng
only has one precious daughter.

144
00:08:24,160 --> 00:08:26,480
If I mess things up, neither of
our families will forgive me.

145
00:08:26,800 --> 00:08:28,200
You're saying that again,
aren't you?

146
00:08:30,440 --> 00:08:33,040
Are you afraid
that our families won't forgive you,

147
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:35,680
or are you afraid of hurting me?

148
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:37,000
I'm afraid of hurting you.

149
00:08:38,720 --> 00:08:39,720
And I'm afraid of failing you.

150
00:08:44,320 --> 00:08:45,320
Yan An,

151
00:08:48,040 --> 00:08:49,839
where do you get the confidence...

152
00:08:49,840 --> 00:08:52,640
to think you could even hurt me?

153
00:08:53,480 --> 00:08:55,400
Is it that I lack charm,

154
00:08:55,560 --> 00:08:56,960
or...

155
00:08:57,760 --> 00:09:00,000
do you think you'll definitely be
the one to have a change of heart?

156
00:09:01,120 --> 00:09:02,120
Let me tell you,

157
00:09:02,480 --> 00:09:04,560
when I was out having fun,

158
00:09:05,520 --> 00:09:09,520
you hadn't even
touched a girl's hand yet.

159
00:09:12,600 --> 00:09:13,600
Where are you going, Zheng You An?

160
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:14,720
Slow down.

161
00:09:15,360 --> 00:09:16,639
- Come here.
- Where are you going?

162
00:09:16,640 --> 00:09:18,120
Don't touch me!

163
00:09:22,040 --> 00:09:23,040
Zheng You An!

164
00:09:23,520 --> 00:09:25,280
I'm warning you for the last time.

165
00:09:26,600 --> 00:09:27,600
From now on,

166
00:09:27,880 --> 00:09:29,000
you are not allowed in my studio.

167
00:09:29,520 --> 00:09:30,800
Otherwise, every time you show up,

168
00:09:31,040 --> 00:09:32,120
I'll hit you!

169
00:09:32,560 --> 00:09:33,600
Self-righteous jerk.

170
00:10:10,640 --> 00:10:12,560
Ms. Dong, have you been busy
painting lately?

171
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,159
I just started a new piece.

172
00:10:14,160 --> 00:10:16,119
Ms. Dong, you're the professional.

173
00:10:16,120 --> 00:10:17,439
Please tell us about this painting.

174
00:10:17,440 --> 00:10:18,880
What exactly is it trying
to express?

175
00:10:18,960 --> 00:10:20,880
Yes. Look at how abstract it is.

176
00:10:20,960 --> 00:10:22,280
What's so good about it?

177
00:10:24,400 --> 00:10:25,480
This piece...

178
00:10:25,600 --> 00:10:28,600
is by a painter from Ethiopia.

179
00:10:29,360 --> 00:10:30,959
The artist's signature style...

180
00:10:30,960 --> 00:10:32,519
is a fusion of New Orientalism...

181
00:10:32,520 --> 00:10:34,160
and Classicism.

182
00:10:34,600 --> 00:10:36,680
There are also
some Abstractist expressions.

183
00:10:37,160 --> 00:10:39,760
As you can see,
the colors are very vibrant.

184
00:10:40,040 --> 00:10:41,400
It has a strong visual impact.

185
00:10:41,840 --> 00:10:42,840
What do you think?

186
00:10:43,160 --> 00:10:44,840
Isn't the painting I just bought
at auction beautiful?

187
00:10:45,480 --> 00:10:46,480
It's beautiful.

188
00:10:47,600 --> 00:10:49,520
It's beautiful, all right,
but we still don't understand...

189
00:10:49,720 --> 00:10:51,360
what it's actually depicting.

190
00:10:51,440 --> 00:10:53,080
Why do you have to understand it?

191
00:10:53,240 --> 00:10:54,240
Have some fruit.

192
00:10:54,840 --> 00:10:56,840
Lan Xiang, I really have to ask you,

193
00:10:57,160 --> 00:10:59,319
what part of this painting
touched you so much...

194
00:10:59,320 --> 00:11:01,279
that you spent
such a fortune to buy it?

195
00:11:01,280 --> 00:11:03,240
- Tell us about it.
- Tell us.

196
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:07,480
Well, what's there to tell?

197
00:11:10,880 --> 00:11:11,880
Come on.

198
00:11:12,440 --> 00:11:14,120
Why are you analyzing this?

199
00:11:15,200 --> 00:11:16,720
Isn't it just a painting?

200
00:11:20,920 --> 00:11:24,400
I... I just looked at the colors.

201
00:11:24,560 --> 00:11:26,200
They're vibrant. It looks good.

202
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:28,360
It was pleasing to the eye,
so I bid on it.

203
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:30,600
I'm so busy every day.

204
00:11:30,601 --> 00:11:32,040
I haven't even looked at it
since I got it.

205
00:11:34,280 --> 00:11:36,240
Ms. Dong, why don't you tell us...

206
00:11:36,440 --> 00:11:39,840
what the artist intended to convey
through this painting?

207
00:11:39,920 --> 00:11:40,920
Yes, Ms. Dong.

208
00:11:42,280 --> 00:11:43,760
Actually, Mrs. Fu...

209
00:11:44,040 --> 00:11:46,880
has already touched upon
the essence of art appreciation.

210
00:11:47,960 --> 00:11:49,840
When we decide to collect a piece,

211
00:11:50,160 --> 00:11:52,920
besides understanding
the artist's skill...

212
00:11:53,280 --> 00:11:55,320
and their style,

213
00:11:55,640 --> 00:11:57,400
we also need to know
their intended message.

214
00:11:57,880 --> 00:12:00,240
However, I believe one can
also completely disregard...

215
00:12:00,440 --> 00:12:01,720
the artist's original intent.

216
00:12:02,040 --> 00:12:03,679
As they say,
"mountains are mountains,"

217
00:12:03,680 --> 00:12:04,680
"and rivers are rivers."

218
00:12:05,080 --> 00:12:06,800
Ultimately, what matters is
our own state of mind.

219
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:09,480
Since this painting caught your eye,

220
00:12:09,800 --> 00:12:11,880
it means it has resonated
with your soul.

221
00:12:14,080 --> 00:12:15,080
Yes, exactly!

222
00:12:15,680 --> 00:12:17,279
That's exactly what I meant.

223
00:12:17,280 --> 00:12:18,399
See?

224
00:12:18,400 --> 00:12:20,080
Ms. Dong explains it so clearly.

225
00:12:21,480 --> 00:12:22,520
Even after all that,

226
00:12:22,760 --> 00:12:24,119
I still can't figure out...

227
00:12:24,120 --> 00:12:25,120
what exactly was painted.

228
00:12:25,280 --> 00:12:26,280
I don't get it either.

229
00:12:27,160 --> 00:12:29,840
That just means you both
need more cultural exposure.

230
00:12:30,360 --> 00:12:32,239
All right.
You all stay here and chat.

231
00:12:32,240 --> 00:12:33,240
Have some fruit.

232
00:12:33,600 --> 00:12:35,320
Don't just stand there.
Come on. Sit down.

233
00:12:35,680 --> 00:12:37,280
Ms. Dong, please teach them more.

234
00:12:45,640 --> 00:12:47,120
- And let me tell you.
- Mrs. Fu.

235
00:12:47,880 --> 00:12:49,440
- Mrs. Fu, do you need help?
- No, it's fine.

236
00:12:50,120 --> 00:12:51,160
Go ahead.

237
00:12:51,440 --> 00:12:52,719
- Mr. Yan.
- Mrs. Fu.

238
00:12:52,720 --> 00:12:54,079
- Please enjoy the drinks
- Go ahead with your work.

239
00:12:54,080 --> 00:12:55,080
I'm so sorry.

240
00:12:55,360 --> 00:12:56,360
Why are you carrying these yourself?

241
00:12:57,680 --> 00:12:58,840
Aren't you sweet?

242
00:13:02,920 --> 00:13:03,920
Did you see?

243
00:13:04,160 --> 00:13:05,160
Mr. Zheng...

244
00:13:05,480 --> 00:13:07,440
and Yan An have been talking
for a while.

245
00:13:08,080 --> 00:13:09,480
Do you think
he's up to something again?

246
00:13:10,840 --> 00:13:13,200
The situation is
getting more and more dire.

247
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:15,320
Mr. Zheng has no other choice.

248
00:13:16,520 --> 00:13:18,480
He's trying his best to grasp...

249
00:13:18,560 --> 00:13:20,400
at this last lifeline.

250
00:13:21,960 --> 00:13:23,519
But he didn't seem...

251
00:13:23,520 --> 00:13:24,760
to like Yan An much in the past.

252
00:13:25,160 --> 00:13:26,160
What else can he do?

253
00:13:26,600 --> 00:13:27,879
Your son was so high-profile...

254
00:13:27,880 --> 00:13:29,200
about announcing his girlfriend.

255
00:13:29,760 --> 00:13:31,280
Mr. Zheng can't
keep chasing after him.

256
00:13:31,800 --> 00:13:34,280
But he shouldn't just turn
to anyone in desperation, right?

257
00:13:35,720 --> 00:13:37,120
Actually, Yan An...

258
00:13:37,520 --> 00:13:38,520
is great in every way,

259
00:13:38,800 --> 00:13:39,960
except he likes
to play around too much.

260
00:13:40,800 --> 00:13:42,840
Does Mr. Zheng even have
any other options now?

261
00:13:45,040 --> 00:13:46,119
Why don't you...

262
00:13:46,120 --> 00:13:47,520
help him think of something?

263
00:13:48,400 --> 00:13:49,400
Do you have another son?

264
00:13:50,920 --> 00:13:51,920
Well,

265
00:13:52,560 --> 00:13:54,560
then I'll try harder
to have another one.

266
00:13:54,800 --> 00:13:56,200
As long as they can wait that long.

267
00:13:58,560 --> 00:13:59,719
Why bring that up again?

268
00:13:59,720 --> 00:14:00,880
You have no sense of occasion.

269
00:14:01,080 --> 00:14:02,160
Look at how scared you are.

270
00:14:03,360 --> 00:14:05,120
Even if I had another son,

271
00:14:05,720 --> 00:14:07,480
I wouldn't want
to be in-laws with his family.

272
00:14:08,840 --> 00:14:09,840
It's a good thing...

273
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:12,360
that our Ming Yu
has a girlfriend now.

274
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:16,200
I really have to thank Xiao Ruan.

275
00:14:16,760 --> 00:14:17,760
Otherwise,

276
00:14:18,480 --> 00:14:20,560
his family would be
all over us, don't you think?

277
00:14:21,680 --> 00:14:22,680
By the way,

278
00:14:22,681 --> 00:14:24,520
our son is going
to bring Xiao Ruan over soon.

279
00:14:24,880 --> 00:14:25,880
You must...

280
00:14:26,440 --> 00:14:28,159
be mindful of
your facial expression.

281
00:14:28,160 --> 00:14:29,280
Don't pull a long face.

282
00:14:29,400 --> 00:14:30,400
Don't scare her.

283
00:14:31,160 --> 00:14:32,680
Forget it. Stop smiling.

284
00:14:32,880 --> 00:14:33,960
- What's wrong?
- That looks terrible.

285
00:14:46,160 --> 00:14:47,160
We're here.

286
00:14:49,720 --> 00:14:50,720
Is it here?

287
00:14:51,760 --> 00:14:52,760
Let's go.

288
00:14:55,640 --> 00:14:56,640
Is your foot okay?

289
00:14:58,280 --> 00:14:59,280
It's fine.

290
00:15:00,600 --> 00:15:01,880
I used to be able
to walk like the wind...

291
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:03,160
even in high heels.

292
00:15:04,800 --> 00:15:05,920
Walk like the wind?

293
00:15:07,760 --> 00:15:09,080
Do you need me to carry you inside?

294
00:15:09,400 --> 00:15:10,400
Don't try to be brave.

295
00:15:11,400 --> 00:15:12,680
I won't give you that chance.

296
00:15:13,720 --> 00:15:14,960
- If you say so.
- I do.

297
00:15:20,440 --> 00:15:21,440
What a good boy.

298
00:15:31,400 --> 00:15:32,400
Dad, Mom.

299
00:15:32,960 --> 00:15:33,960
We're not late, are we?

300
00:15:35,280 --> 00:15:36,520
Old Fu, come here.

301
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:38,200
Come here. Stop chatting!

302
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:41,000
Dad, Mom.

303
00:15:41,640 --> 00:15:43,800
Let me introduce you.
This is my girlfriend, Ruan Si Xian.

304
00:15:45,200 --> 00:15:46,440
This is Chairman Fu, my dad.

305
00:15:46,960 --> 00:15:47,960
Hello, Chairman Fu.

306
00:15:48,280 --> 00:15:49,280
Hello.

307
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:51,040
This is Ms. He.

308
00:15:51,600 --> 00:15:52,600
You've met her before.

309
00:15:52,640 --> 00:15:53,640
She's my mom.

310
00:15:53,880 --> 00:15:55,760
Ms. Ruan, hello.

311
00:15:56,080 --> 00:15:57,080
We meet again.

312
00:15:58,160 --> 00:16:01,720
I just happen
to have a son who is...

313
00:16:02,680 --> 00:16:03,680
around your age.

314
00:16:09,240 --> 00:16:10,280
You look beautiful today.

315
00:16:10,760 --> 00:16:11,760
Hello, Ms. He.

316
00:16:12,840 --> 00:16:13,960
What happened just now?

317
00:16:14,640 --> 00:16:16,160
She almost twisted her ankle.
It's okay.

318
00:16:16,560 --> 00:16:17,639
Are you all right?

319
00:16:17,640 --> 00:16:18,679
I'm fine.

320
00:16:18,680 --> 00:16:19,720
You look so pretty.

321
00:16:20,480 --> 00:16:21,480
Everyone, come over here!

322
00:16:22,520 --> 00:16:23,520
Ms. Dong, come here.

323
00:16:23,640 --> 00:16:24,679
Come here, quickly.

324
00:16:24,680 --> 00:16:26,519
Come on, hurry up.
Let me formally introduce you.

325
00:16:26,520 --> 00:16:27,679
- A formal introduction?
- Come here, everyone.

326
00:16:27,680 --> 00:16:28,920
- Who is it? Why so formal?
- Look.

327
00:16:29,840 --> 00:16:32,200
This is my son's girlfriend,
Ruan Si Xian.

328
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:34,000
Isn't she pretty?

329
00:16:34,600 --> 00:16:36,040
Ms. Ruan looks so beautiful today.

330
00:16:37,760 --> 00:16:40,840
Oh, right. And this is Ms. Dong,
the famous painter.

331
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,000
Mom.

332
00:16:52,120 --> 00:16:53,120
Long time no see.

333
00:17:07,440 --> 00:17:08,440
Long time no see.

334
00:17:09,480 --> 00:17:10,480
You look lovely today.

335
00:17:15,920 --> 00:17:17,280
Right, let me introduce you.

336
00:17:17,840 --> 00:17:19,160
This is Mr. Zheng.

337
00:17:19,760 --> 00:17:20,760
He's You An's father.

338
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:24,960
Hello.

339
00:17:26,040 --> 00:17:27,040
Zheng Tai Chu.

340
00:17:29,200 --> 00:17:30,200
An An's father.

341
00:17:49,200 --> 00:17:50,240
Why isn't it him?

342
00:17:52,840 --> 00:17:53,840
Hello, sir.

343
00:17:59,360 --> 00:18:00,560
I really didn't expect this.

344
00:18:01,240 --> 00:18:02,240
Ms. Dong,

345
00:18:02,320 --> 00:18:04,600
I didn't know Xiao Ruan was
your daughter too.

346
00:18:05,920 --> 00:18:06,920
No wonder.

347
00:18:08,880 --> 00:18:10,040
The more I look,
the more alike you look.

348
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:29,440
Are you bored?
Have something to eat.

349
00:18:35,320 --> 00:18:37,000
What's wrong? You look troubled.

350
00:18:37,640 --> 00:18:39,280
Why haven't I seen your mother?

351
00:18:39,720 --> 00:18:40,720
My mom?

352
00:18:42,240 --> 00:18:44,599
Maybe my mom is busy
with something else.

353
00:18:44,600 --> 00:18:45,880
But I haven't seen her...

354
00:18:46,280 --> 00:18:47,360
since the banquet started.

355
00:18:47,880 --> 00:18:48,880
It's okay.

356
00:18:49,080 --> 00:18:50,440
Maybe she'll come back
once she's finished...

357
00:18:50,680 --> 00:18:51,680
with whatever she's doing.

358
00:18:53,440 --> 00:18:55,280
Is she a bit unhappy?

359
00:18:57,240 --> 00:18:58,240
Don't overthink it.

360
00:18:58,880 --> 00:19:00,200
Then she must not like me.

361
00:19:01,880 --> 00:19:02,920
Was I...

362
00:19:03,400 --> 00:19:05,080
a bit too out of line today?

363
00:19:08,520 --> 00:19:09,520
I don't think so.

364
00:19:10,200 --> 00:19:11,920
Besides, you only told the truth.

365
00:19:12,520 --> 00:19:14,160
Hasn't Ms. Dong
always been your mother?

366
00:19:14,640 --> 00:19:15,640
I admit,

367
00:19:16,440 --> 00:19:17,440
today,

368
00:19:17,840 --> 00:19:19,640
I was being a bit of a prankster.

369
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:21,200
Isn't that perfect?

370
00:19:22,240 --> 00:19:24,200
That way, you and my mom are even.

371
00:19:24,760 --> 00:19:26,040
Did you forget last time,

372
00:19:26,280 --> 00:19:27,280
when she tried to introduce...

373
00:19:27,440 --> 00:19:29,720
her "somewhat handsome" son to you?

374
00:19:30,920 --> 00:19:31,920
Right.

375
00:19:33,760 --> 00:19:34,760
But your mom...

376
00:19:35,080 --> 00:19:37,560
must be hiding because she's upset.

377
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:40,000
Go and find her.

378
00:19:40,760 --> 00:19:41,760
I'm not going.

379
00:19:41,960 --> 00:19:43,360
If she's upset, she has my dad.

380
00:19:43,720 --> 00:19:45,040
My most important task now...

381
00:19:45,400 --> 00:19:46,760
is to keep my girlfriend company.

382
00:19:47,440 --> 00:19:49,039
- Have some fruit.
- No.

383
00:19:49,040 --> 00:19:50,080
- Go, now.
- I'm not going.

384
00:19:53,480 --> 00:19:54,680
Goldie.

385
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:56,760
What kind of luck do I have?

386
00:19:57,760 --> 00:19:59,159
No matter how hard
I try to avoid it,

387
00:19:59,160 --> 00:20:00,160
I still can't escape it.

388
00:20:01,520 --> 00:20:03,560
How did I end up in this situation?

389
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:14,080
What's wrong?

390
00:20:14,840 --> 00:20:15,840
Me?

391
00:20:17,920 --> 00:20:19,000
The moment I see you,

392
00:20:19,440 --> 00:20:21,080
my blood pressure skyrockets.

393
00:20:21,440 --> 00:20:22,600
It's higher than your head.

394
00:20:23,440 --> 00:20:24,440
Fine.

395
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:25,640
Then you should rest.

396
00:20:25,880 --> 00:20:26,880
I'll leave you alone.

397
00:20:27,480 --> 00:20:28,480
Stop right there.

398
00:20:30,640 --> 00:20:31,640
Sit down.

399
00:20:31,840 --> 00:20:33,000
- Sit down!
- Okay.

400
00:20:36,160 --> 00:20:37,160
Tell me the truth.

401
00:20:38,360 --> 00:20:39,679
Did you know all along...

402
00:20:39,680 --> 00:20:41,040
that she's Dong Xian's daughter?

403
00:20:44,320 --> 00:20:45,320
You rascal.

404
00:20:46,160 --> 00:20:47,720
Why didn't you tell me sooner?

405
00:20:48,120 --> 00:20:49,880
- You knew that she and I...
- I know.

406
00:20:50,360 --> 00:20:52,040
But I'm dating Ruan Si Xian,

407
00:20:52,280 --> 00:20:53,280
not her mother.

408
00:20:53,320 --> 00:20:55,840
Don't give me
that declaration of Independence.

409
00:20:56,240 --> 00:20:59,000
Of course, it would be best
to have our parents' blessing.

410
00:20:59,520 --> 00:21:00,640
But even if I don't,

411
00:21:01,160 --> 00:21:02,200
I'm still going to be with her.

412
00:21:08,200 --> 00:21:09,920
My head is spinning.

413
00:21:10,440 --> 00:21:12,840
Did I ever say I wouldn't
let you two be together?

414
00:21:14,200 --> 00:21:15,360
I just find it strange.

415
00:21:15,680 --> 00:21:18,559
Why do you insist
on being Dong Xian's son-in-law?

416
00:21:18,560 --> 00:21:19,680
Why?

417
00:21:20,960 --> 00:21:21,960
Mom,

418
00:21:21,961 --> 00:21:23,079
it's not that I insist on being...

419
00:21:23,080 --> 00:21:25,040
Ms. Dong's son-in-law.

420
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:27,960
It's that I'll only marry
Ruan Si Xian.

421
00:21:32,480 --> 00:21:33,920
- Mom.
- Don't look at me like that.

422
00:21:34,400 --> 00:21:35,400
I'm not falling for it.

423
00:21:38,440 --> 00:21:40,320
Mom, don't be mad.

424
00:21:40,560 --> 00:21:42,519
Don't you actually
really like Ruan Si Xian?

425
00:21:42,520 --> 00:21:44,439
Liking her is one thing,

426
00:21:44,440 --> 00:21:46,160
but she's Dong Xian's daughter.

427
00:21:47,640 --> 00:21:49,319
Yes, she's Dong Xian's daughter.

428
00:21:49,320 --> 00:21:50,320
But it doesn't matter.

429
00:21:50,560 --> 00:21:51,679
I like her.

430
00:21:51,680 --> 00:21:52,960
It's not because of her mother.

431
00:21:54,440 --> 00:21:55,600
But son,

432
00:21:56,160 --> 00:21:58,160
you should have told me sooner.

433
00:21:58,600 --> 00:22:00,720
You should've let me prepare myself.

434
00:22:00,960 --> 00:22:01,960
Look at you two.

435
00:22:02,360 --> 00:22:04,240
Just when I was feeling most proud,

436
00:22:04,720 --> 00:22:05,720
you hit me with this.

437
00:22:07,080 --> 00:22:08,119
My head...

438
00:22:08,120 --> 00:22:10,000
I don't feel
comfortable anywhere right now.

439
00:22:10,760 --> 00:22:12,680
In that regard,
I really didn't think it through.

440
00:22:13,440 --> 00:22:14,800
I sincerely apologize to you.

441
00:22:17,000 --> 00:22:18,360
Mom, don't be angry anymore.

442
00:22:18,680 --> 00:22:20,280
I actually have
another little secret.

443
00:22:20,680 --> 00:22:22,080
- Do you want to hear it?
- Stay away from me.

444
00:22:23,440 --> 00:22:24,440
Sit over there and talk.

445
00:22:27,800 --> 00:22:28,880
Speaking of this secret,

446
00:22:30,400 --> 00:22:31,400
actually, Ruan Ruan...

447
00:22:31,640 --> 00:22:32,640
and Ms. Dong...

448
00:22:33,080 --> 00:22:34,960
have some bad blood
between them.

449
00:22:36,880 --> 00:22:37,880
Forget it.

450
00:22:38,640 --> 00:22:40,280
What bad blood could there be
between a mother and daughter?

451
00:22:40,560 --> 00:22:42,119
Is it as bad
as the knot in my heart?

452
00:22:42,120 --> 00:22:43,280
You're actually right.

453
00:22:44,480 --> 00:22:45,640
The issue between them...

454
00:22:45,800 --> 00:22:47,880
is much bigger than the one
between you and Ms. Dong.

455
00:22:49,240 --> 00:22:50,360
- Really?
- Of course.

456
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:53,000
Why is that?

457
00:22:54,400 --> 00:22:55,440
Actually, this matter...

458
00:22:56,120 --> 00:22:57,120
is a long story.

459
00:23:03,640 --> 00:23:04,880
You haven't
eaten anything all night.

460
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:08,000
This is very good.

461
00:23:08,440 --> 00:23:09,560
It's low in sugar.

462
00:23:13,280 --> 00:23:14,280
Are you okay?

463
00:23:16,360 --> 00:23:17,360
There's nothing wrong.

464
00:23:18,640 --> 00:23:19,640
At least,

465
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:21,120
she called me "Mom" today.

466
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:24,000
I didn't expect her...

467
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:26,000
to be all grown up now.

468
00:23:26,280 --> 00:23:27,280
Actually, back then,

469
00:23:27,520 --> 00:23:29,120
when I divorced her father,

470
00:23:30,080 --> 00:23:31,560
I already knew this day would come.

471
00:23:33,600 --> 00:23:34,600
It's just that,

472
00:23:35,600 --> 00:23:37,040
with her attitude toward me,

473
00:23:38,480 --> 00:23:40,240
I still feel a bit conflicted.

474
00:23:40,760 --> 00:23:41,760
I understand.

475
00:23:42,760 --> 00:23:43,880
I wonder,

476
00:23:44,880 --> 00:23:46,160
what has she been through
all these years?

477
00:23:48,840 --> 00:23:51,320
I never expected her
to be with Ming Yu now.

478
00:23:54,440 --> 00:23:55,480
It's actually quite nice.

479
00:23:59,840 --> 00:24:01,640
By the way, is An An okay?

480
00:24:01,920 --> 00:24:03,440
She has known Si Xian
for a long while.

481
00:24:03,560 --> 00:24:04,680
I never told her.

482
00:24:05,080 --> 00:24:06,400
- Will she...
- It's okay.

483
00:24:07,120 --> 00:24:08,200
Let her process it on her own.

484
00:24:09,280 --> 00:24:10,280
I...

485
00:24:11,200 --> 00:24:12,760
just want you to be okay.

486
00:24:33,360 --> 00:24:34,360
What are you spacing out for?

487
00:24:41,280 --> 00:24:42,280
What do you see in it?

488
00:24:43,920 --> 00:24:44,920
Chaos.

489
00:24:46,640 --> 00:24:47,640
The painting is chaotic,

490
00:24:48,920 --> 00:24:49,920
and my heart is even more so.

491
00:24:52,640 --> 00:24:53,640
Tell me about it.

492
00:24:54,160 --> 00:24:55,440
Maybe I can help you vent a little.

493
00:24:58,600 --> 00:24:59,720
You really can't help me with this.

494
00:25:00,800 --> 00:25:01,800
My heart is in such a mess,

495
00:25:03,560 --> 00:25:05,320
and you played a major part in it.

496
00:25:09,320 --> 00:25:11,720
- Zheng You An.
- Why couldn't they just tell me?

497
00:25:22,120 --> 00:25:23,120
They...

498
00:25:25,040 --> 00:25:26,280
probably had their reasons.

499
00:25:26,920 --> 00:25:28,080
In my view,

500
00:25:29,240 --> 00:25:30,640
if they don't tell me something,

501
00:25:31,080 --> 00:25:33,560
it means they don't trust me at all.

502
00:25:34,800 --> 00:25:35,800
Don't say that.

503
00:25:36,440 --> 00:25:37,440
Maybe they were protecting you.

504
00:25:38,120 --> 00:25:39,680
Then the protection period
expired tonight.

505
00:25:51,000 --> 00:25:52,319
Now that you mention it,

506
00:25:52,320 --> 00:25:53,360
I've figured it out.

507
00:25:54,240 --> 00:25:56,679
So just now, Xiao Ruan wasn't
lashing out at me.

508
00:25:56,680 --> 00:25:57,879
Of course not.

509
00:25:57,880 --> 00:25:59,479
She was aiming
at her mother, Dong Xian.

510
00:25:59,480 --> 00:26:00,480
Yes.

511
00:26:03,320 --> 00:26:04,320
But that still doesn't make sense.

512
00:26:04,760 --> 00:26:05,760
What doesn't make sense?

513
00:26:05,840 --> 00:26:09,120
Look, Dong Xian might
be a bit snobby,

514
00:26:09,440 --> 00:26:10,560
but she's a good person.

515
00:26:10,760 --> 00:26:11,760
- Yes.
- Look.

516
00:26:12,040 --> 00:26:13,960
An An isn't
even her biological daughter,

517
00:26:14,080 --> 00:26:15,200
yet she's so good to her.

518
00:26:15,680 --> 00:26:17,400
She's so attentive,
down to the last detail.

519
00:26:18,120 --> 00:26:19,120
When parents divorce,

520
00:26:19,440 --> 00:26:20,480
she might not want her husband,

521
00:26:20,920 --> 00:26:23,000
but it's not like she wouldn't
want her own biological daughter.

522
00:26:25,520 --> 00:26:26,520
As a mother,

523
00:26:27,120 --> 00:26:28,200
one's heart is always soft.

524
00:26:28,520 --> 00:26:29,640
Children are...

525
00:26:29,920 --> 00:26:32,039
the result of 10 months
of pregnancy...

526
00:26:32,040 --> 00:26:33,360
and the flesh of our own flesh.

527
00:26:34,200 --> 00:26:35,240
We love them dearly.

528
00:26:35,880 --> 00:26:38,279
So when it comes
to her own daughter,

529
00:26:38,280 --> 00:26:39,280
is it the opposite?

530
00:26:39,800 --> 00:26:40,800
This isn't right. No.

531
00:26:41,160 --> 00:26:42,160
This...

532
00:26:48,560 --> 00:26:49,560
You rascal.

533
00:26:50,880 --> 00:26:52,160
Are you making up stories for me?

534
00:26:52,400 --> 00:26:53,760
Are you trying to fool your mom?

535
00:26:54,560 --> 00:26:56,240
Making things up? I wouldn't dare.

536
00:26:56,600 --> 00:26:57,600
Truly?

537
00:26:59,080 --> 00:27:00,080
See for yourself
if you don't believe me.

538
00:27:01,360 --> 00:27:02,360
Ruan Ruan.

539
00:27:03,200 --> 00:27:05,280
Isn't she standing there
all by herself?

540
00:27:05,720 --> 00:27:06,720
She looks so lonely.

541
00:27:07,120 --> 00:27:08,120
Look.

542
00:27:09,200 --> 00:27:10,200
She really does.

543
00:27:10,800 --> 00:27:11,800
She...

544
00:27:12,480 --> 00:27:14,560
has a deep-seated family trauma.

545
00:27:16,480 --> 00:27:18,160
But she rarely mentions it to me.

546
00:27:19,000 --> 00:27:20,000
I only know...

547
00:27:20,440 --> 00:27:21,600
that to attend the aviation academy,

548
00:27:22,320 --> 00:27:24,440
she sold the old house
that her father gave her.

549
00:27:26,400 --> 00:27:27,440
- Really?
- It's true.

550
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:29,000
She even asked just now,

551
00:27:30,120 --> 00:27:31,840
"Is your mom mad at me?"

552
00:27:32,120 --> 00:27:33,240
"Does she not like me?"

553
00:27:33,760 --> 00:27:35,240
That's why she asked me to come up
to keep you company.

554
00:27:37,360 --> 00:27:38,440
- Really?
- Of course.

555
00:27:38,800 --> 00:27:40,280
- Look.
- Did she really say that?

556
00:27:40,840 --> 00:27:41,840
I wouldn't lie to you.

557
00:27:46,320 --> 00:27:48,080
- I really do like Xiao Ruan.
- Yes.

558
00:27:48,840 --> 00:27:49,840
You have good taste.

559
00:27:53,080 --> 00:27:55,079
When Ruan Si Xian
called her "Mom" today,

560
00:27:55,080 --> 00:27:56,520
it was indeed hard to take.

561
00:27:57,520 --> 00:27:58,920
But she wasn't targeting you.

562
00:27:59,280 --> 00:28:00,280
You were just caught
in the crossfire.

563
00:28:00,600 --> 00:28:02,240
Fine, stop making excuses for her.

564
00:28:02,800 --> 00:28:03,800
It's not that I don't understand.

565
00:28:04,360 --> 00:28:06,280
Her own mother,

566
00:28:06,400 --> 00:28:07,919
instead of staying by her side,

567
00:28:07,920 --> 00:28:09,280
went to be a mother
to someone else.

568
00:28:10,360 --> 00:28:11,520
She has her reasons...

569
00:28:12,320 --> 00:28:13,320
for hating me.

570
00:28:13,680 --> 00:28:14,959
Who could possibly accept that?

571
00:28:14,960 --> 00:28:15,960
Why would she hate you?

572
00:28:15,961 --> 00:28:17,400
It's not like you're the one
who made her parents divorce.

573
00:28:19,760 --> 00:28:20,880
Can you please get out?

574
00:28:21,560 --> 00:28:23,079
Weren't you having a good talk
with my dad?

575
00:28:23,080 --> 00:28:24,120
Just leave already.

576
00:28:24,200 --> 00:28:25,240
Can you let me be alone for a while?

577
00:28:26,120 --> 00:28:27,999
What did I say wrong this time?

578
00:28:28,000 --> 00:28:29,000
Stop bothering me.

579
00:28:29,280 --> 00:28:30,280
- Go.
- Wait.

580
00:28:30,720 --> 00:28:32,160
Where am I supposed to go?

581
00:28:33,240 --> 00:28:34,440
Are you two looking at paintings?

582
00:28:34,960 --> 00:28:36,120
- Mrs. Fu.
- Mrs. Fu.

583
00:28:37,720 --> 00:28:40,080
Well, why don't you two
go outside for a drink?

584
00:28:40,600 --> 00:28:41,600
Take a stroll.

585
00:28:41,920 --> 00:28:42,920
I want to chat with An An for a bit.

586
00:28:43,320 --> 00:28:45,320
- Okay, we'll head out then.
- Go on.

587
00:28:51,720 --> 00:28:52,720
You go first.

588
00:28:55,280 --> 00:28:56,600
How is it? Is everything okay?

589
00:28:57,720 --> 00:28:58,720
She's fine.

590
00:28:58,920 --> 00:28:59,920
Were you nervous?

591
00:29:00,880 --> 00:29:02,360
Are you still joking
at a time like this?

592
00:29:04,840 --> 00:29:07,040
Are you afraid my mom won't
approve of our relationship?

593
00:29:12,560 --> 00:29:13,720
I'm starting to regret it.

594
00:29:15,120 --> 00:29:16,120
At first,

595
00:29:17,640 --> 00:29:19,040
I wanted to embarrass my mom.

596
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:21,840
But I ended up
hurting so many people.

597
00:29:22,520 --> 00:29:24,640
It was never my intention
to hurt anyone.

598
00:29:26,200 --> 00:29:28,240
I thought this spiteful revenge
would feel good,

599
00:29:29,480 --> 00:29:30,480
but now,

600
00:29:31,000 --> 00:29:32,000
I only feel guilty.

601
00:29:41,080 --> 00:29:42,400
I can understand
everything you've said.

602
00:29:43,800 --> 00:29:45,000
But you really don't need
to feel guilty.

603
00:29:46,280 --> 00:29:48,640
But your mom was kind enough
to invite me to your home.

604
00:29:49,400 --> 00:29:50,400
In the end,

605
00:29:50,880 --> 00:29:52,160
I just came here to ruin everything.

606
00:29:57,760 --> 00:29:58,760
You know,

607
00:29:59,680 --> 00:30:01,880
I am unconditionally
and always on your side.

608
00:30:03,480 --> 00:30:04,480
Really?

609
00:30:04,720 --> 00:30:05,720
Of course it's true.

610
00:30:08,480 --> 00:30:10,040
Actually, it's all thanks to you.

611
00:30:11,440 --> 00:30:13,399
Since this painting
entered our home,

612
00:30:13,400 --> 00:30:15,359
this is the first time...

613
00:30:15,360 --> 00:30:16,720
I've sat here and truly admired it.

614
00:30:19,160 --> 00:30:21,200
Tell me, why are these paintings
so expensive?

615
00:30:22,440 --> 00:30:25,120
Spending this much money
really hurts my wallet.

616
00:30:25,600 --> 00:30:26,920
I'd rather buy jewelry.

617
00:30:29,840 --> 00:30:32,039
But I just wanted to show off...

618
00:30:32,040 --> 00:30:33,040
in front of your mother for once.

619
00:30:33,320 --> 00:30:35,160
It's her fault for always
snatching the paintings I want.

620
00:30:35,520 --> 00:30:36,520
Right?

621
00:30:38,720 --> 00:30:41,640
However, your mother was
quite right about one thing.

622
00:30:42,480 --> 00:30:43,560
Appreciating art...

623
00:30:44,480 --> 00:30:45,959
is about seeing mountains
as mountains...

624
00:30:45,960 --> 00:30:46,960
and rivers as rivers.

625
00:30:47,440 --> 00:30:48,719
I don't understand the art,

626
00:30:48,720 --> 00:30:49,760
but I understand the principle.

627
00:30:50,320 --> 00:30:52,520
Isn't that just
the three stages of enlightenment?

628
00:30:54,040 --> 00:30:56,520
First, seeing mountains as mountains
and rivers as rivers.

629
00:30:56,960 --> 00:30:58,799
Then, seeing mountains not
as mountains...

630
00:30:58,800 --> 00:31:00,080
and rivers not as rivers.

631
00:31:01,120 --> 00:31:03,640
Congratulations,
you're more advanced than me.

632
00:31:03,760 --> 00:31:06,000
You've already reached
the second stage.

633
00:31:06,280 --> 00:31:07,280
Me?

634
00:31:08,880 --> 00:31:11,840
Why do I see mountains not
as mountains...

635
00:31:12,000 --> 00:31:13,200
and rivers not as rivers?

636
00:31:13,800 --> 00:31:15,800
Because you're overthinking things.

637
00:31:17,800 --> 00:31:19,560
You've started
to question everything.

638
00:31:20,880 --> 00:31:23,240
It's just like when we look
at a painting.

639
00:31:25,440 --> 00:31:27,079
We always fixate on the details.

640
00:31:27,080 --> 00:31:28,840
By obsessing over those details,

641
00:31:29,440 --> 00:31:30,440
the more you look,

642
00:31:30,441 --> 00:31:32,000
the more you lose sight
of the painting's essence.

643
00:31:32,440 --> 00:31:34,600
That's how misunderstandings
are born.

644
00:31:36,240 --> 00:31:37,519
Misunderstanding a painting...

645
00:31:37,520 --> 00:31:38,880
and misunderstanding
a person's heart.

646
00:31:42,400 --> 00:31:44,000
But it's okay.

647
00:31:44,360 --> 00:31:45,960
There's a third level of insight.

648
00:31:46,280 --> 00:31:48,640
Seeing mountains as mountains
and rivers as rivers.

649
00:31:50,760 --> 00:31:51,760
Don't be afraid.

650
00:31:52,120 --> 00:31:53,560
Sincerity is sincerity.

651
00:31:53,960 --> 00:31:55,839
It won't just vanish because of...

652
00:31:55,840 --> 00:31:58,040
a little misunderstanding
or unpleasantness.

653
00:31:58,280 --> 00:31:59,280
It won't.

654
00:32:00,880 --> 00:32:02,440
There, there. Don't feel sad.

655
00:32:05,520 --> 00:32:06,640
Aren't I quite impressive too?

656
00:32:07,640 --> 00:32:09,920
Let me tell you, usually,
I'm just too low-key.

657
00:32:10,120 --> 00:32:12,720
I don't like to be flashy.
I don't like to show off.

658
00:32:15,360 --> 00:32:17,280
Mrs. Fu, what you're saying...

659
00:32:18,040 --> 00:32:19,040
is a great philosophy.

660
00:32:19,320 --> 00:32:20,840
It's all connected to art.

661
00:32:21,160 --> 00:32:22,399
That's my philosophy too.

662
00:32:22,400 --> 00:32:24,360
It makes me
sound more profound, doesn't it?

663
00:32:26,480 --> 00:32:27,480
Okay, there.

664
00:32:27,960 --> 00:32:28,960
There now.

665
00:32:29,800 --> 00:32:30,800
Don't cry anymore.

666
00:32:37,280 --> 00:32:38,800
You had such nice toys as a kid.

667
00:32:39,240 --> 00:32:40,240
You even had your own swing.

668
00:32:41,840 --> 00:32:43,040
I didn't exactly
catch the good times.

669
00:32:45,000 --> 00:32:46,480
When my family first moved here,

670
00:32:47,760 --> 00:32:48,760
I had already finished grad school.

671
00:32:49,560 --> 00:32:50,800
This swing you see here...

672
00:32:51,640 --> 00:32:53,360
was installed
because Ms. He insisted.

673
00:32:55,200 --> 00:32:56,600
She's quite young at heart.

674
00:32:57,600 --> 00:32:58,640
But it's hard on my dad.

675
00:32:59,640 --> 00:33:01,200
Every time my mom wants
to go on the swing,

676
00:33:01,680 --> 00:33:02,880
my dad has to push her.

677
00:33:03,760 --> 00:33:05,040
Does Chairman Fu
actually agree to that?

678
00:33:06,320 --> 00:33:07,520
He wouldn't dare refuse.

679
00:33:12,880 --> 00:33:13,880
Want to give it a try?

680
00:33:23,200 --> 00:33:24,480
This is the first time...

681
00:33:25,040 --> 00:33:26,280
I haven't had
to wait in line for a swing.

682
00:33:27,240 --> 00:33:28,719
When I wanted to swing as a kid,

683
00:33:28,720 --> 00:33:29,720
I always had to wait in line.

684
00:33:30,240 --> 00:33:31,840
Every time I was the last in line,

685
00:33:32,640 --> 00:33:34,120
if the kids in front didn't want
to get off,

686
00:33:34,960 --> 00:33:35,960
I wouldn't get a turn.

687
00:33:37,080 --> 00:33:39,120
But my dad would wait with me.

688
00:33:40,480 --> 00:33:41,760
When it was finally my turn,

689
00:33:42,240 --> 00:33:43,520
he would push me on the swing.

690
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:46,160
When I had had enough,

691
00:33:46,520 --> 00:33:47,520
he would walk me home.

692
00:33:48,480 --> 00:33:49,520
But I remember this one time.

693
00:33:50,160 --> 00:33:52,080
I had just finished
eating beef hot pot at home.

694
00:33:53,160 --> 00:33:54,640
I was so happy that day.

695
00:33:56,080 --> 00:33:58,040
After eating, I dragged my dad...

696
00:33:58,480 --> 00:33:59,480
to the swings.

697
00:34:00,040 --> 00:34:02,240
I swung so hard that day,

698
00:34:02,560 --> 00:34:04,240
I felt like I was flying
into the sky.

699
00:34:05,800 --> 00:34:06,800
And guess what?

700
00:34:08,640 --> 00:34:10,519
All that beef hot pot I had eaten...

701
00:34:10,520 --> 00:34:11,760
got thrown up.

702
00:34:12,240 --> 00:34:13,760
I ended up crying all the way home.

703
00:34:16,520 --> 00:34:17,960
Did you like swinging that much?

704
00:34:20,200 --> 00:34:21,360
I really did.

705
00:34:22,680 --> 00:34:23,680
But after I grew up,

706
00:34:24,240 --> 00:34:25,240
I never played on them again.

707
00:34:26,080 --> 00:34:28,040
Every time I saw a swing,
I would walk around it.

708
00:34:29,480 --> 00:34:30,680
Later, when I went
to the aviation academy,

709
00:34:31,600 --> 00:34:32,640
I started training
on the spiraling swing.

710
00:34:33,520 --> 00:34:34,520
Everyone else complained,

711
00:34:35,160 --> 00:34:36,240
but I actually enjoyed it.

712
00:34:37,680 --> 00:34:38,680
It was great.

713
00:34:38,760 --> 00:34:39,840
I could fly into the sky again.

714
00:35:13,720 --> 00:35:15,080
Isn't pushing the swing...

715
00:35:15,640 --> 00:35:16,640
really tiring?

716
00:35:24,960 --> 00:35:25,960
I never tire of it.

717
00:36:53,200 --> 00:36:54,200
Are you that happy?

718
00:36:54,520 --> 00:36:55,520
Of course.

719
00:36:56,400 --> 00:36:57,400
This necklace...

720
00:36:57,760 --> 00:36:58,760
is actually from your mother.

721
00:37:00,240 --> 00:37:01,439
My mom said it can
be considered a gift...

722
00:37:01,440 --> 00:37:02,440
for meeting you for the first time.

723
00:37:03,200 --> 00:37:04,360
But it's far too valuable.

724
00:37:05,040 --> 00:37:06,040
Do you still think...

725
00:37:06,520 --> 00:37:07,520
she doesn't like you?

726
00:37:08,280 --> 00:37:10,000
She's just being kind for your sake.

727
00:37:11,640 --> 00:37:12,960
This dress...

728
00:37:13,040 --> 00:37:14,360
wasn't picked out
by your mother too, was it?

729
00:37:14,600 --> 00:37:17,000
I am a grown man
with normal aesthetic taste.

730
00:37:17,880 --> 00:37:19,360
This doesn't seem like your style.

731
00:37:20,680 --> 00:37:21,680
It really doesn't.

732
00:37:22,000 --> 00:37:23,160
I actually prefer another outfit.

733
00:37:23,680 --> 00:37:24,680
Which one?

734
00:37:24,840 --> 00:37:25,840
Your uniform.

735
00:37:41,160 --> 00:37:42,160
Purser, time to clock out.

736
00:38:03,960 --> 00:38:06,160
You just met someone
who let you down.

737
00:38:07,000 --> 00:38:08,960
If you want to find someone
who won't let you down...

738
00:38:09,160 --> 00:38:10,400
or betray you,

739
00:38:11,600 --> 00:38:12,600
that person can only be yourself.

740
00:38:24,560 --> 00:38:25,640
Hello, I've arrived.

741
00:38:27,360 --> 00:38:28,360
I see you, sir.

742
00:38:28,520 --> 00:38:29,520
I'm coming to you now.

743
00:39:33,240 --> 00:39:34,440
- Coffee.
- Thank you.

744
00:39:35,120 --> 00:39:36,120
Don't drink too much...

745
00:39:39,520 --> 00:39:40,520
coffee.

746
00:39:59,120 --> 00:40:03,240
(Hengshi Question Database,
Regulations)

747
00:40:19,880 --> 00:40:22,440
- Go home.
- "To learn and to practice..."

748
00:40:22,520 --> 00:40:23,560
- Go home.
- "Is it not..."

749
00:41:09,040 --> 00:41:10,320
(Fan Speed)

750
00:41:28,200 --> 00:41:30,560
You always have the same problem.

751
00:41:30,680 --> 00:41:32,440
No matter how many times I tell you,
you never remember.

752
00:41:33,920 --> 00:41:36,040
Aren't you being
a bit too gentle today?

753
00:41:36,240 --> 00:41:37,520
What happened to being extra harsh?

754
00:41:38,280 --> 00:41:39,280
This afternoon,

755
00:41:40,000 --> 00:41:41,000
I'll be extra harsh.

756
00:41:57,120 --> 00:41:58,120
Long time no see.

757
00:41:58,640 --> 00:41:59,640
Long time no see.

758
00:42:04,760 --> 00:42:06,240
Are you here to wait for me?

759
00:42:07,280 --> 00:42:08,280
Don't get the wrong idea.

760
00:42:08,600 --> 00:42:10,080
I'm here to see Xiao Ruan.

761
00:42:12,720 --> 00:42:13,720
Okay.

762
00:42:17,840 --> 00:42:20,120
I think it's necessary
to explain something to you.

763
00:42:21,800 --> 00:42:23,039
Lately, Ruan Si Xian and I,

764
00:42:23,040 --> 00:42:24,759
other than having
some interactions at work,

765
00:42:24,760 --> 00:42:26,280
have had almost no contact.

766
00:42:27,000 --> 00:42:28,160
You two are colleagues.

767
00:42:28,360 --> 00:42:29,360
It's normal to have interactions.

768
00:42:31,800 --> 00:42:32,800
Then why are you looking for her?

769
00:42:33,880 --> 00:42:34,880
I'm planning to resign.

770
00:42:35,160 --> 00:42:36,680
- I'm here to give her a small gift.
- Are you crazy?

771
00:42:38,480 --> 00:42:39,800
You're doing so well
at work right now.

772
00:42:40,360 --> 00:42:42,439
Or did you find an airline
with better pay?

773
00:42:42,440 --> 00:42:43,639
Are you planning to jump ship?

774
00:42:43,640 --> 00:42:44,839
I want to go back to school.

775
00:42:44,840 --> 00:42:45,999
Jiang Zi Yue,
your ideas are really...

776
00:42:46,000 --> 00:42:47,000
Captain Yue.

777
00:42:50,800 --> 00:42:51,800
I'll leave you to it.

778
00:42:59,960 --> 00:43:01,720
Jiang Zi Yue, don't you think
you're being a bit too naive?

779
00:43:03,840 --> 00:43:05,320
We're both adults now.

780
00:43:05,600 --> 00:43:07,480
How can you have
such unrealistic ideas?

781
00:43:07,760 --> 00:43:08,760
Yue Yang,

782
00:43:08,920 --> 00:43:09,920
it seems that after all this time,

783
00:43:10,520 --> 00:43:11,600
you still don't know me very well.

784
00:43:12,880 --> 00:43:14,320
At least until today,

785
00:43:14,800 --> 00:43:16,200
"naive" was never a word
that applied to me.

786
00:43:16,600 --> 00:43:19,200
Naive doesn't apply to you,
but resigning does.

787
00:43:20,400 --> 00:43:22,640
If you go to school now,
you'll have to find a job later.

788
00:43:22,720 --> 00:43:24,119
And then, by the time you graduate,

789
00:43:24,120 --> 00:43:26,039
you won't even know
what the world has become.

790
00:43:26,040 --> 00:43:27,200
You'll have to start all over again.

791
00:43:27,520 --> 00:43:29,799
And think about it, when you have
no income, what will your family do?

792
00:43:29,800 --> 00:43:30,800
Do you think...

793
00:43:36,400 --> 00:43:38,360
So you've known
about my family situation all along.

794
00:43:43,720 --> 00:43:48,680
(Departing Ep. 18 for Ep. 19)
